Load Test Suite
===============

Benchmarks spine throughput against a fleet of simulated SNMP devices
running under snmpsim in Docker. MariaDB is port-mapped to the host so
the local spine binary runs natively without a container.

Prerequisites
-------------

- Python 3.8 or later in PATH
- Docker with Compose v2 (docker compose, not docker-compose)
- mysql client in PATH (MariaDB or MySQL, used only to seed the DB)
- spine binary built at the repo root:

    cd /path/to/spine
    ./configure && make

  The benchmark script looks for the binary at ../../spine relative to
  this directory. Override with SPINE_BIN=/path/to/spine.

Quick start
-----------

    cd tests/load
    sh run-bench.sh

This generates 500 fake devices, starts MariaDB on 127.0.0.1:3307 and
snmpsim on 127.0.0.1:16100/udp, then runs spine at 10, 25, and 50
threads. Docker services are torn down automatically on exit.

Options
-------

    --count N          number of simulated devices (1-508, default: 500)
    --threads T1,T2,T3 comma-separated thread counts (default: 10,25,50)

Environment overrides:

    COUNT=100 THREAD_COUNTS=5,10 sh run-bench.sh

Output
------

The script prints a throughput table after all runs complete:

    threads | devices | items | duration_s | results | throughput (items/s)
    --------+---------+-------+------------+---------+--------------------
         10 |     500 |  2500 |       45.2 |    2500 |                55
         25 |     500 |  2500 |       18.7 |    2500 |               133
         50 |     500 |  2500 |       11.3 |    2500 |               221

Columns:

  threads      spine --threads value for this run
  devices      total host rows in the DB
  items        total poller_item rows (devices x 5 OIDs each)
  duration_s   wall-clock seconds from spine launch to exit
  results      SELECT COUNT(*) FROM poller_output after the run
  throughput   items / duration_s

A results value less than items means spine did not poll all devices
within the run. Check spine stderr for timeout or connection errors.

snmpsim performance ceiling
---------------------------

snmpsim is single-threaded and handles roughly 400-600 requests per
second on typical hardware. At high spine thread counts (50+) snmpsim
becomes the bottleneck, not spine. The throughput numbers therefore
reflect the snmpsim ceiling rather than spine's true capacity.

To measure spine's own ceiling, replace snmpsim with real devices or
a multi-process SNMP simulator. The infrastructure here is useful for
regression testing (does throughput stay the same across spine builds?)
rather than absolute capacity planning.

File layout
-----------

    gen-snmprec.py        generates one .snmprec file per device IP
    gen-seed.py           generates seed SQL (host + poller_item rows)
    run-bench.sh          orchestrates the full benchmark
    docker-compose.load.yml  MariaDB + snmpsim with host port mappings
    snmprec/              populated by gen-snmprec.py at runtime
    load-seed.sql         generated at runtime, removed on exit
    spine.conf.load       generated at runtime, removed on exit

IP ranges used: 192.0.2.1-254 and 198.51.100.1-254 (RFC 5737).
